t;,469769226,&amp;quot;Helvetica&amp;quot;,335551500,&amp;quot;0&amp;quot;,268442635,&amp;quot;22&amp;quot;]}&quot;&gt;Role&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-parastyle=&quot;Body&quot;&gt; Summary&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-parastyle=&quot;Body&quot;&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:120}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Director, Thought Leader Liaison develops and executes a strategic engagement model with external thought leaders in rare neuromuscular diseases to support Dyne’s commercial objectives. This role builds credible, compliant, and value-driven relationships with neuromuscular experts and advocates, translating insights into actionable commercial strategy. The role serves as a senior external-facing representative of Dyne, shaping disease-state understanding, treatment adoption, and long-term success of Dyne’s neuromuscular portfolio, and will be responsible for defined activities within the Northeast TLL region.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;TextRun SCXW5903375 BCX8&quot; lang=&quot;EN-US&quot; data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW5903375 BCX8&quot;&gt;This is a field-based position.&amp;nbsp; Candidates must &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW5903375 BCX8&quot;&gt;reside&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW5903375 BCX8&quot;&gt; within the assigned territory and within reasonable driving distance of a major commercial airport capable of supporting frequent regional and national travel.&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;EOP Selected SCXW5903375 BCX8&quot; data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:240,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-ccp-border-between=&quot;0px none #000000&quot; data-ccp-padding-between=&quot;0px&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-parastyle=&quot;Body&quot;&gt;Primary Responsibilities include:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:120}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Thought Leader Strategy &amp;amp; Engagement&lt;/em&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develops and executes a comprehensive thought leader engagement strategy focused on rare neuromuscular diseases, aligned with Dyne’s commercial and portfolio priorities.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identifies, profiles, and prioritizes national and regional neuromuscular thought leaders based on&amp;nbsp;expertise, influence, and strategic relevance.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Builds and sustains long-term, trust-based relationships with clinicians and experts treating rare neuromuscular disorders through compliant, value-driven engagement.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serves as a credible commercial partner in discussions related to disease state education, evolving treatment paradigms, and unmet needs in neuromuscular disease.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Insight Generation &amp;amp; Strategic Activation&lt;/em&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Captures, synthesizes, and translates insights from neuromuscular thought leaders into actionable recommendations for brand, launch, and lifecycle strategy.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provides strategic input into positioning, messaging, and tactical planning that reflects the unique dynamics of rare disease diagnosis, treatment, and patient journeys.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitors KOL insights related to current and future market dynamics and competitive intelligence through customer meetings, congresses, advisory boards, and analytics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shares insights with commercial leadership and cross-functional partners to inform decision-making and&amp;nbsp;optimize&amp;nbsp;execution.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Congress, Advisory Board &amp;amp; Peer-to-Peer Engagement&lt;/em&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leads commercial engagement strategy for key neuromuscular congresses, including pre-, during-, and post-meeting planning and follow-up.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Designs and executes advisory boards, speaker programs, and peer-to-peer educational initiatives focused on rare neuromuscular disease education.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identifies and recruits appropriate KOLs for content development and other marketing projects, such as web content, training, handouts, and related materials.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partners cross-functionally to ensure consistency, effectiveness, and compliance across engagement forums.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Cross-Functional Leadership &amp;amp; Governance&lt;/em&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborates and interfaces regularly across regions and with multiple departments, including Sales, Marketing, Medical Affairs, Market Access, Training, Legal, and Compliance, to ensure aligned and compliant execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manages vendor partnerships as needed, including medical education agencies, meeting services providers, and other external partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establishes metrics to assess effectiveness, impact, and ROI of thought leader engagement activities.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensures all interactions adhere to regulatory, legal, and company compliance standards.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-charstyle=&quot;Strong&quot;&gt;E&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-charstyle=&quot;Strong&quot;&gt;d&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-charstyle=&quot;Strong&quot;&gt;ucation and Skills Requirements:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree&amp;nbsp;required; advanced degree preferred.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of experience in biotechnology or pharmaceutical commercial roles, with experience in rare disease or specialty markets strongly preferred.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience engaging neuromuscular or rare disease thought leaders in a commercial context.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of the rare disease commercialization landscape, including diagnosis complexity, referral dynamics, and patient advocacy.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to translate complex scientific and clinical insights into clear, innovative, and actionable commercial strategies. Self-starter with the ability to deliver results in therapeutic areas with high unmet need.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent interpersonal, oral, and written communication skills, with strong execution focus and executive presence, and the ability to influence without authority.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong cross-functional collaboration skills and experience&amp;nbsp;operating&amp;nbsp;in matrixed organizations.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated commitment to ethical, compliant engagement practices.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to manage a large geographical territory.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Domestic travel up to 80% is&amp;nbsp;required.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LI-Remote&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;MA Pay Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$230,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$260,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
